      "Formats commit messages using Conventional Commits types, scopes, subjects, bodies, and trailers.",
      "Provides examples for feature, fix, docs, refactor, test, build, CI, chore, style, perf, and revert commits.",
      "Supplies pull request titles, descriptions, review checklists, and test plan sections.",
      "Guides common Git workflows including branching, rebasing, cherry-picking, stashing, bisecting, pulling, and pushing.",
      "Explains daily workflow steps for preparing, reviewing, merging, and cleaning branches."
